{% doc %}
  A store policy's page (/policies/…), laid out as a page without a hero (DS-177): the page
  header, then the policy's text as page text. Shopify gives these pages no template and its own
  markup, so the layout renders this in its place. The text is the store's (Settings, Policies);
  .gs-prose neutralises fonts pasted from Word, as on every page (§6.11).

  @param {object} policy - The policy, from shop.policies. Required

  @example
  {%- render 'gs-policy', policy: policy -%}
{% enddoc %}
<div class="gs-container gs-lead-in">
  <header class="gs-page-head">
    {%- render 'gs-title-block', title: policy.title -%}
  </header>
</div>
{%- if policy.body != blank -%}
  <div class="gs-section gs-surface-paper">
    <div class="gs-container">
      <div class="gs-prose">{%- render 'gs-rich-text', html: policy.body -%}</div>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
